From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 08:15:55 -0400
Subject: add Arc's second pin tier: pinned within a Space

The first DMG treated Chromium's pin as "above all Spaces", which is Arc's
essentials tier; Arc's ordinary pin is per-Space, sits above the Clear line,
and survives Clear. The operator called the missing tier out.

SpaceModel now carries it: IsSpacePinned/SetSpacePinned by tab handle,
persisted in per-tab session extra data next to the tab's Space and collected
on restore through the same parked user data. Clear skips Space-pinned tabs.
Pinning moves the tab to the top of the unpinned block, directly under the
Clear line, which is where the tier lives visually.

The toggle is a pair of tab context menu items -- Pin to This Space / Unpin
from This Space -- rather than one toggle, because the menu model cannot ask
per-tab checked state; the tab strip collection controller enables exactly one
of the pair from the window's SpaceModel and executes both. The model's own
command switches treat the pair as no-ops, so nothing changes for windows
without Spaces.

Why: the two tiers are how Arc's sidebar is actually organised; with one tier
the essentials row and the pinned section could not both exist.
Removable when: never, short of dropping Spaces.
